    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 176</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_176/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 05 Feb 2025 00:45:26 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_176/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code? Why?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;&#xA;type People interface {&#xA;    Show()&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;type Student struct{}&#xA;&#xA;func (stu *Student) Show() {&#xA;&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;&#xA;    var s *Student&#xA;    if s == nil {&#xA;        fmt.Println(&amp;#34;s is nil&amp;#34;)&#xA;    } else {&#xA;        fmt.Println(&amp;#34;s is not nil&amp;#34;)&#xA;    }&#xA;    var p People = s&#xA;    if p == nil {&#xA;        fmt.Println(&amp;#34;p is nil&amp;#34;)&#xA;    } else {&#xA;        fmt.Println(&amp;#34;p is not nil&amp;#34;)&#xA;    }&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;s is nil&#xA;p is not nil&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Remember, an interface type value is &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt; if and only if both its dynamic value and dynamic type are &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 140</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_140/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 24 Dec 2024 23:28:20 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_140/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {  &#xA;    var i interface{}&#xA;    if i == nil {&#xA;        fmt.Println(&amp;#34;nil&amp;#34;)&#xA;        return&#xA;    }&#xA;    fmt.Println(&amp;#34;not nil&amp;#34;)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. nil&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. not nil&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;A &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/rtD7YmJZxp1&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Simply put, an interface variable has two values: one is its type, and the other is its value.&#xA;For an &lt;code&gt;if&lt;/code&gt; interface, the &lt;code&gt;live() == nil&lt;/code&gt; condition is true only when both the value and the type are zero values.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
