      <description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code compile?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (&#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;type worker interface {&#xA;    work()&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;type person struct {&#xA;    name string&#xA;    worker&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    var w worker = person{}&#xA;    fmt.Println(w)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A: Yes;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B: No;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C: Don&amp;rsquo;t know&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Answer: A &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/RSSWTD3otlJ&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;01&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;01&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#01&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We all know Go doesn&amp;rsquo;t have inheritance, but it can simulate some inheritance features through embedded types. It&amp;rsquo;s important to remember that interfaces are also types, and naturally, they can be used as embedded types. If the &lt;code&gt;person&lt;/code&gt; struct in the problem were changed to:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
